  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home Improvement",
    tags: [
      "best caulk for windows",
      "exterior window caulk",
      "window caulk",
      "best caulk for window trim",
      "caulk for window frames"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Window Sealant Picks
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Caulk <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">for Windows</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Six window sealants chosen for the two jobs a window has: a weatherproof seal between the frame and the siding outside, and a clean, paintable line at the trim inside.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#osi-quad-max"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            See the Picks
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Shaheer Ali Khan</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Consumer Product Testing &amp; Materials Performance Specialist</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="11.4k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#how-we-chose" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. How We Chose</a>
          <a href="#exterior-vs-interior" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Exterior vs Interior Window Caulk</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Our 6 Picks</a>
          <a href="#movement" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Movement Ratings Explained</a>
          <a href="#cold-weather" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Caulking Windows in Cold Weather</a>
          <a href="#paint" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Painting Window Caulk</a>
          <a href="#what-not-to-caulk" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Where Not to Caulk a Window</a>
          <a href="#prep-and-application" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Prep and Application</a>
          <a href="#how-long-it-lasts" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. How Long Window Caulk Lasts</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The best caulk for windows depends on which side of the glass you are standing on. Outside, the joint between the frame and the siding needs a high-movement sealant that bonds to vinyl, aluminum and wood and shrugs off rain and sun. Inside, the trim needs a fast, paintable caulk that leaves a clean line. Buy one product for each job and both will last; buy one tube for everything and one of them will fail.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="how-we-chose" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. How We Chose
          </h2>

          <p>
            We did not lab-test these sealants. This is a researched buying guide, and every figure on the product cards comes from the manufacturer's technical data sheet, product page or label, with retailer specification tables used only where the maker's own document was silent. Where sources disagree, we give both figures and tell you which one to plan around.
          </p>

          <p>
            We split the job in two before choosing products. The exterior joint between a window frame and the siding is a weatherproofing seal that has to move with the house through heat, cold and rain. The interior gaps between casing, jamb and wall are cosmetic: they need a clean, paintable line and very little movement capability. One product rarely does both jobs well.
          </p>

          <p>
            For exterior picks, we prioritized movement rating, the range of temperatures the sealant can be applied in, adhesion to vinyl, aluminum, wood and masonry, and paintability. For interior trim, we looked at paint-ready time, ease of tooling and cleanup. We kept this list separate from our <a href="/best-exterior-caulk/">best exterior caulk</a> roundup, which covers siding and general exterior gaps; the products below are chosen specifically for windows.
          </p>

          <p>
            We also checked each product against its version and name, because sealant lines are confusing. DAP sells Dynaflex 230, Dynaflex Ultra and Dynaflex Ultimate; GE sells several Paintable Silicone Supreme versions; Loctite's window sealant is also sold as PL S40. The specs on our cards belong to the exact product named.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="exterior-vs-interior" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Exterior vs Interior Window Caulk
          </h2>

          <p>
            Exterior window caulk seals the joint where the frame meets the siding or masonry. It keeps wind-driven rain out of the wall, and it has to survive ultraviolet light, temperature swings and the frame and siding expanding and contracting at different rates. That calls for a true sealant with a stated movement rating, such as OSI Quad Max, DAP Dynaflex Ultra, GE Paintable Silicone Supreme or Loctite PL Window, Door and Siding.
          </p>

          <p>
            Interior window caulk fills the cosmetic gaps around trim: between the casing and the wall, the casing and the jamb, and sometimes the stool. These joints barely move and stay dry, so the priority is a clean bead that takes paint quickly. A paintable acrylic latex such as DAP Alex Fast Dry is the right tool, and it costs a fraction of an exterior sealant.
          </p>

          <p>
            The common mistake is using interior caulk outside. Basic acrylic latex is cheap and easy, which is why so many exterior window joints get it, and it is also why so many of those joints crack and open within a couple of seasons. Our guide to <a href="/silicone-vs-latex-caulk/">silicone vs latex caulk</a> explains why the chemistry matters outdoors.
          </p>

          <p>
            The reverse mistake is less common but annoying: using pure silicone on interior trim you plan to paint. Standard silicone repels paint, leaving a shiny bead that never matches the trim. If you must use silicone indoors, choose a paintable hybrid or keep it to places that will not be painted.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What about the glass?</h3>

          <p>
            Window caulk goes around the frame, not on the glass itself. The seal between glass and sash is part of the window unit, and on modern windows it should not be caulked over. If the glass seal has failed, which usually shows as fog between panes, that is a window repair or replacement job, not a caulking job.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Our 6 Picks
          </h2>

          <p>
            We did not lab-test these sealants. Every movement rating, temperature range, paint window and cure time below comes from the maker's technical data sheet, product page or label, and where sources disagree we say which figure to trust. Four picks are for the exterior frame joint, one is a clear option for stained or colored frames, and one is for interior trim.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
